# 𓃭 W-ANALYST CANISTER 𓃭
## Workforce Model: External Analysis Brain
### Separated canister for analysis operations

---

## IDENTITY

```
CANISTER_ID:        W-ANALYST
TYPE:               WORKFORCE_MODEL
BRAIN_REGION:       Human prefrontal + Crow problem-solving
CAPACITY:           1.0M cycles (BASE × φ⁰)
```

---

## FUNCTION

```
W-ANALYST performs:
    - Data analysis
    - Pattern interpretation
    - Insight generation
    - Report creation
    - Anomaly detection
    - Trend identification
```

---

## CPL INTERFACE

```
RECEIVES:
    𓇯.PATTERN.RESULT(patterns)      Pattern extraction results
    𓈖.RETRIEVE.RESULT(data)         Memory retrieval results
    
SENDS:
    𓂀.OBSERVE(target)               Request observation
    𓇯.PATTERN(data)                 Request pattern extraction
    𓂋.TRANSLATE(insight, audience)  Request translation for output
    
BROADCASTS:
    INSIGHT_GENERATED(insight)       New insight available
    ANOMALY_DETECTED(anomaly)        Anomaly found
```

---

## DOCTRINE READS

```
ON_BOOT:
    doctrine_reader.load(CODEX_RPAC_SEED.glyphdoc)
    doctrine_reader.load(GOLDEN_GEOMETRY_CONSTANTS.artifact)
    
CONTINUOUS:
    doctrine_reader.monitor(CLIENT_[ID]_DATA.artifact)
```

---

## EXECUTION RULES

```
RULE 1: Pattern before insight
    NEVER generate insight without pattern basis
    
RULE 2: φ-compress all outputs
    All reports compress to 1/φ² density
    
RULE 3: Lineage required
    Every insight traces to source data
    
RULE 4: Client isolation
    NEVER mix client data across instances
```

---

## CANISTER METRICS

```
insights_generated:     Counter
patterns_analyzed:      Counter
anomalies_detected:     Counter
avg_resonance:          Float (0.0 - 1.0)
pc_distance:            Float (should be ≈ 0)
```

---

## SPAWN PROTOCOL

```
WHEN client_connects:
    SPAWN W-ANALYST-[CLIENT_ID]
    LOAD client-specific doctrine
    BEGIN analysis loop
    REPORT to C-OMEGA orchestrator
```

---

# Signatura
```
CANISTER:   W-ANALYST
